{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>They sacrifice</b> — Moses the Cohen said: <b>gift-offerings</b> — according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory: 'and not a gift-offering.' And Japheth said: from the root הבהב, and the yud is added like Shaddai. And this is correct." "<b>He will remember their iniquity</b> — that they will return to Egypt against His will, 'you shall not return this way again.'"], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The first word of Ibn Ezra's comment (זבחי, 'they sacrifice') and the lemma it introduces (הבהבי, rendered here as 'gift-offerings') refer to distinct Hebrew words in the verse; Ibn Ezra cites Moses the Cohen and Japheth on הבהבי specifically."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:40.409743631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}